[step] The broad compliant wall is set in from the receiver edge. This 0.500 mm offset compares its side boundary with the receiver exterior; the actual side clearance is qualified separately in toolpath-review.json. The long wall stays 1.30 mm thick.
click: x=0.500 y=1.200 z=24.070

[step] The flexible wall's fore surface is inset 0.550 mm from the receiver's exterior plane. The offset provides its prescribed bending room; it does not interrupt the retained key-bearing shoulders. The actual 0.60 mm fore relief is verified in the commanded road envelopes.
click: x=7.000 y=0.550 z=24.295

[sliver] This is the 13 mm-wide upper edge of the intentional 1.30 mm broad spring wall. It prints vertically from its integral root and follows the accepted PET-GF faucet-cover wall pattern. Snap force and permanent set still require the coupon trial.
click: x=7.000 y=1.200 z=41.820

[ceiling] The key windows retain their square working faces. Native toolpath supports are exposed through the open windows and rear release opening; separate the fore/aft branches and remove them before mating. The long hidden wall relief contains no support sheet. See toolpath-review.json and its section figure.
